From e958587fae10e7d42dc4efea84d1b833038306e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 00:13:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] outputconfigurationstore: keep touching outputs touching
 across mode/scale changes

Output positions are stored as independent absolute pixel coordinates, so
when one output's mode or scale changes, nothing recomputes any other
output's position. An arrangement where e.g. two monitors' top corners
were deliberately placed touching drifts into a gap or an overlap the
moment either output's effective size changes.

Detect when outputs are touching (corner-to-corner, edge-centered, or with
a deliberate residual offset) each time a Setup is stored, and record that
relationship instead of only the absolute position. When building an
OutputConfiguration from stored state (setupToConfig, generateConfig), or
when a caller hands us one directly (Workspace::applyOutputConfiguration,
which is what a live scale/mode change from the KCM or an application
actually goes through), re-derive any anchored output's position from its
target's current position and size rather than reusing the stale stored
value.

The anchor is inferred from whatever arrangement is already in place -
there's no new UI for it - and is additive to the stored config format, so
existing kwinoutputconfig.json files keep loading exactly as before.
